WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.734
-Welcome back.
-Thank you so much.

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:05.100
-It is fan-- It is great
to see you in person.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.868
-I know. Last time,
I was on Zoom with you.

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:08.567
-Zoomers, Zooming,
but I appreciate you

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:09.868
doing that for us.
-And no masks.

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.434
And now we're no masks.
The people are here.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:16.400
-This is amazing.
Hi, guys!

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.934
-You look fantastic.
-Thank you.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.167
-I'm happy you're here.

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:21.434
And I asked you to play
"VR Pictionary" tonight.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:22.834
-Yes.
-You were very nice,

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:24.467
and you said yes,
but you were very honest,

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:25.667
and you said,
"I just want to let you know,

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.033
I'm terrible at drawing."

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:29.968
-There are very few things
that give me major anxiety,

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:33.267
and drawing is one of --
I am terrible at drawing.

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:36.267
I cannot draw a stick figure.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.601
-Well, to prove this,
you brought a photo

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:40.067
that you drew.
-Okay.

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.100
Well, wait.
Let me give context.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.467
-Before we see it -- Yeah.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.367
-So, during COVID,
my friend group,

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.701
we were doing
all these online games together,

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:50.334
and a lot was Pictionary
and Charades and all this stuff.

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:51.901
And one of the games
was a drawing game,

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:54.334
and we had to make
a self-portrait,

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:56.200
and this one was mine.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.734
-Okay. I-I --
You guys be the judge.

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.234
I don't know.
Is this that bad?

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:02.901
This is, uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.634
-So...
Thank you!

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:07.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.801
So...
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:12.300
I had a high ponytail
that day, and I was wearing --

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.634
You were the Genie in "Aladdin"
for an off-Broadway version.

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:19.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.334 --> 00:01:22.434
-My assistant still
has this as my caller I.D.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:24.234
[ Laughter ]
Literally!

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:25.567
-I'm gonna say
you have to use this.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.734
-Oh, she uses it for everything.
-You have to post this.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:30.601
-She's on the verge of getting
fired for how often she uses it.

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:32.567
Let me tell you.
-That's so funny.

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:34.234
-So that's my
drawing capabilities.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:36.334
-Yeah, well, I appre--
Well, I appreciate you

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:38.033
doubly playing the game.
You're a good sport.

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:40.067
-You're welcome.
-I saw you at the Emmys

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:41.434
a couple weeks ago.
-Yeah.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.701
-Looking gorgeous, as always.
-Oh, thank you so much.

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:44.901
-Ooh, la la.
-Thank you.

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:46.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:49.400
-Beautiful.
-They literally cut that dress

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.767
before I walked out.

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:52.701
That was a full gown.
-What?

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:55.534
-And they just -- we cut it.
We went wild.

00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:56.767
-Wait. So it was
just gonna be all...

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:59.467
-It was all long.
No leg.

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:01.968
-And we cut it.
-And then you said, "All leg."

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:03.868
-Yeah, and then we just cut it
before I walked --

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:05.601
Can you imagine the insanity

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:06.868
of doing that
before I walked out?

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:08.601
-I love that you did that.
-I know! We just cut it.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:10.000
-Isn't that the best to just go,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.667
"I'm just gonna take this risk
and see what's up"?

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:13.667
-Yeah, you could do that
with your suit pants.

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:14.968
You could just cut them
before you come out.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:17.801
You never know.
-We'll get there.

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:20.334
We got a long -- got a long
season ahead of us.

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:22.133
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:24.100
Congrats. You were nominated
for your show,

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.901
"The Flight Attendant."
You're fantastic in it.

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:28.467
-Thank you.
-Congratulations.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:31.033
-Thanks, guys.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:33.734
-Well, Sharon Stone plays --
played your mom

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:36.868
in a few episodes,
and you posted this,

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:38.734
you and Sharon,
and I just want to say that

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.067
I was once in a movie

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:42.000
where Sharon Stone
played my mother...

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.968
-You know, I heard this.
-...in a flashback.

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:46.167
It wasn't me.
It was a kid, a little boy,

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:48.300
but his mom was Sharon Stone.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.200
-It's almost like
we're TV related.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.133
-Yeah, kind of. Right?
-TV mom.

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:54.501
-My mother -- my real mother
in real life,

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:55.901
was, like, over the moon.

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:59.634
She was like, "Finally!
This is the best casting ever!"

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:00.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:03.634
"I am Sharon Stone!"
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:06.534
-It's so funny that you bring
your mom up because,

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.734
when I posted that --
So, I was like the first person

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:11.300
to announce
that Sharon was on our show.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.234
So I posted that picture
that you just showed.

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:16.467
And what I wrote in my --
what I wrote was,

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:18.334
"Finally, the cat's
out of the bag.

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:20.801
@SharonStone.
Hi, Mom."

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:23.000
And that night, I was looking
through the comments,

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.234
and my real mom
was the top comment,

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:26.801
and she put, "Hi!"

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:28.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.801 --> 00:03:32.734
I had to text her, like,
"Mom, you can just text me."

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:34.000
-"We're not
having a conversation."

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.467
-Talking about Sharon.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:39.000
It was so funny.
I didn't know if she was

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.467
being geniously hilarious,

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:42.601
or she really was just like,
"That's me!"

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:44.367
-Yeah, of course.
-Yeah, I don't know.

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:46.167
Either way, it made me laugh.
-You can't beat moms, right?

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:47.300
-No.
-They're the greatest.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.200
-The best.
-You were sitting at the Emmys

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.334
with your boyfriend, who --
a friend of our show, too.

00:03:52.334 --> 00:03:53.367
-Yes.
-Tom Pelphrey.

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:55.868
-Yes.
-Just amazing on "Ozark."

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.534
-So good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.534 --> 00:04:01.033
I know.
-Uh...

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:02.567
How did you two meet?

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:04.868
-So, we actually --
we have the same manager.

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:07.501
This is a very Hollywood story.
I know.

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:08.934
We have the same manager.
-No, I like it.

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:11.601
-And actually, I was just
shooting a film in Berlin.

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:14.167
And about six months --
even longer, nine months ago,

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.167
my manager was submitting
different clients

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:18.801
and had asked me
if I knew who Tom was.

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:20.801
And she goes,
"And side note, he's single."

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:22.367
This was a while ago.
-Yeah.

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:24.334
-And I was like,
"Oh, I'm not ready to date.

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:25.567
And I don't know
who we're casting."

00:04:25.567 --> 00:04:27.234
And I didn't even know
who he was.

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:28.601
And I had told my sister,
I'm like,

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:29.901
"Do you know this
Tom Pelphrey?" she's like,

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:31.534
[ Gasps ]
"Have you seen 'Ozark'?!"

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:33.167
-Oh, my gosh!
-And I was like,

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:35.067
"No, I haven't!"
-"Have you seen 'Ozark'?!"

00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:36.834
-No, I think I'm the only one
that hasn't seen it,

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.334
and they were like,
"How can you not see 'Ozark'?!"

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:40.601
-Yeah, exactly.
-People lose their mind.

00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:42.534
-Oh, I know. I was that person
for a long time.

00:04:42.534 --> 00:04:43.968
-It's crazy.
-I mean, on the other end.

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:45.434
I was with you.
-Like, psychos.

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:47.501
-People will freak out.
They go, "You haven't even --"

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:49.300
Yeah, Jason Bateman
yelled at me --

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.901
"You haven't seen 'Ozark'?!"
-I know!

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:53.100
[ Laughter ]
God, back off.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.033
-Yeah, but...
-So, anyway...

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:57.501
The months had gone on,
and we had never met,

00:04:57.501 --> 00:04:59.834
and I was out here
promoting "Flight Attendant"

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:02.767
with that same manager,
who's his manager,

00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:04.834
and she's like, "I'm going to
the 'Ozark' premiere tonight.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:06.100
Do you want to come with me?"

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:07.734
And it didn't even occur to me,
and I was like,

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:08.968
"Yeah, I'll go."

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:11.167
So I got all dressed up,
and I was standing there,

00:05:11.167 --> 00:05:13.767
and I was at the bathroom,
and I was waiting.

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:16.634
And I hear this voice.
It was Tom, and he's like,

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:18.200
"Where's this Kaley?"
And I was like,

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.968
"Where's this Kaley?"
And I turned around,

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:22.267
and it was Tom, and it was like
[ Vocalizing ]

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:24.734
It was like love at first sight.

00:05:24.734 --> 00:05:26.767
That was --
The world stopped.

00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:28.200
-Oh, I love that.
-I know.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.567
-I love that.
It's a great story.

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:31.667
-It was really sweet, yeah.
-Well, you guys looked

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:33.667
great together at the Emmys.
-And I still have to pee.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:36.234
I never went to the bathroom.
-Never went to the bathroom.

00:05:36.234 --> 00:05:37.701
-Yeah, had to pee
that whole night.

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:39.801
I want to talk about your movie.
Let's talk about "Meet Cute."

00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:43.667
-Yeah, "Meet Cute."
-Now, "Meet Cute," in the --

00:05:43.667 --> 00:05:46.968
I only learned about this
when I think it was on

00:05:46.968 --> 00:05:50.434
after "Saturday Night Live,"
is a term for, in a script

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:52.968
when the two people,
that the romantic leads meet.

00:05:52.968 --> 00:05:56.067
-It's like an accident,
like, a cute way to meet.

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:57.400
I mean, meet cu--
-Yeah.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.200
That's what a meet cute --
Yeah, I mean I had to --

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.100
I didn't know what that was.
-I didn't, either,

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.234
and I kept saying, "This doesn't
really roll off the tongue."

00:06:03.234 --> 00:06:04.901
And then we said it
so many times

00:06:04.901 --> 00:06:07.400
that I was like,
"Okay, whatever. It's fine."

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.000
-The movie is a --
-It's a meet cute.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.601
-Is exactly a meet cute.
-Yes.

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:14.067
-And so you're meeting
the very cute Pete Davidson.

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:15.567
-Yes. Yes.
-So it's you and Pete.

00:06:15.567 --> 00:06:17.067
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:20.167
Yeah, no, he was great.
He actually -- meeting him

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:22.634
in real life was
an interesting situation.

00:06:22.634 --> 00:06:23.934
-Have you known Pete or...?
-No.

00:06:23.934 --> 00:06:26.234
So, he was attached
to this film way before I was.

00:06:26.234 --> 00:06:28.834
And so when I actually attached,
obviously everyone was like,

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:31.200
"You guys need to meet.
We hope that there's chemistry."

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.934
Like, we had never met, ever.

00:06:32.934 --> 00:06:34.701
So, we get in contact,
and he was in L.A.

00:06:34.701 --> 00:06:35.734
for a few days and, like, "Okay.

00:06:35.734 --> 00:06:36.934
Maybe we should meet
for a coffee.

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:39.033
Let's meet the director."
Like, I had never met him

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:40.734
or anything, hadn't talked
to him about the project.

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:42.968
So I find out
that he would like to meet me,

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:45.367
but he wanted to meet me
in an escape room.

00:06:45.367 --> 00:06:47.601
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:48.734
And I'm like,
"You know what, Pete?

00:06:48.734 --> 00:06:50.934
Not everyone
has to end up on TMZ."

00:06:50.934 --> 00:06:52.834
[ Laughter ]
Like, Oh, my gosh, like...

00:06:52.834 --> 00:06:55.267
I'm like,
"Why can't anything be normal?"

00:06:55.267 --> 00:06:56.801
So I'm like, "Am I --"
-Pete, that's funny.

00:06:56.801 --> 00:06:59.567
-Yeah. So we did.
Me, the director, and Pete,

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:01.868
I met him in an escape room.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.868 --> 00:07:03.734
-That's an interesting way
to meet someone.

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:05.234
-You really can learn
a lot about someone

00:07:05.234 --> 00:07:07.000
in an escape room, yeah.
-How is --

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.934
How are you, and how is Pete
in an escape room?

00:07:09.934 --> 00:07:12.701
-I don't enjoy escape rooms.
I like answers.

00:07:12.701 --> 00:07:14.801
I don't want to know why
there's a 6 on the ceiling

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:17.167
and why it connects to the bike
that opens the door.

00:07:17.167 --> 00:07:19.667
I hate that. Like, just, like,
"Get me out of here."

00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:23.434
-You're out of there, yeah.
-Yeah, Pete just laughs a lot.

00:07:23.434 --> 00:07:25.234
I don't even know if he knows
what he's laughing at.

00:07:25.234 --> 00:07:27.300
-Yeah, yeah.
He's just a happy guy.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.067
-He's a happy guy.
-He's a happy human being.

00:07:29.067 --> 00:07:30.667
-Very happy.
-But you do get to know

00:07:30.667 --> 00:07:32.167
how someone
reacts under pressure.

00:07:32.167 --> 00:07:34.667
And would you ever do
an escape room again?

00:07:34.667 --> 00:07:35.934
-Yes. In fact, my next co-star

00:07:35.934 --> 00:07:37.267
I'm going to bring
to that escape room

00:07:37.267 --> 00:07:38.834
so I look like a genius
because I'm gonna get out.

00:07:38.834 --> 00:07:40.767
I know exactly how to get out.
-That is brilliant.

00:07:40.767 --> 00:07:42.067
-Yeah.
So, thank you, Pete.

00:07:42.067 --> 00:07:43.901
-That's actually a good move.

00:07:43.901 --> 00:07:45.067
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:45.067 --> 00:07:46.868
Here's Kaley Cuoco
in "Meet Cute."

00:07:46.868 --> 00:07:48.300
Take a look at this.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.434
-Thirsty?

00:07:50.434 --> 00:07:51.834
-Hmm?

00:07:51.834 --> 00:07:54.400
-Uh, for a drink.
Not -- Not sexually.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:55.968
Gross. I didn't --
I didn't mean it like --

00:07:55.968 --> 00:07:57.434
I'm gonna order
an alcoholic beverage.

00:07:57.434 --> 00:07:59.801
Would you like to have
one, too, with me?

00:07:59.801 --> 00:08:02.067
-Uh, s-sure. W-Why not?
-Yeah?

00:08:02.067 --> 00:08:03.434
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:08:03.434 --> 00:08:05.100
Great.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:09.033
[ Clears throat ]

00:08:09.033 --> 00:08:11.400
[ Clears throat ] Phil?
-What can I get you?

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:13.167
-Old Fashioned.
-Old Fashioned.

00:08:13.167 --> 00:08:14.567
[ Both laugh ]

00:08:14.567 --> 00:08:16.434
-How adorable.

00:08:16.434 --> 00:08:18.634
There's a real cute vibe
going on here.

00:08:18.634 --> 00:08:21.567
-Two Old Fashioneds,
and you can cut that out, Phil.

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:23.434
Hi. I'm Sheila.
-Hi.

00:08:23.434 --> 00:08:25.567
-Hi.
I'm, uh -- I'm Gary.

00:08:25.567 --> 00:08:27.167
-Oh, Gary.
Wow.

00:08:27.167 --> 00:08:29.400
So we both have,
like, old-timey names.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.801
-Yeah, I guess.

00:08:30.801 --> 00:08:32.801
Very sadistic parents.

00:08:32.801 --> 00:08:34.200
-Oh.
Don't even get me started.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.634
I mean, there's
no couch in here.

00:08:35.634 --> 00:08:38.567
[ Laughs ]

00:08:38.567 --> 00:08:39.934
Kaley Cuoco, everybody!

00:08:39.934 --> 00:08:43.968
"Meet Cute" premieres tomorrow
exclusively on Peacock.

